id: pm-gh1475
title: "GH-1475: settle authenticated lossless merges within one reviewed delivery"
description: Published 2026.10.14 losslessly merges disjoint scalar edits and union collections but leaves a pending receipt and gate-failing health until explicit reconcile plus a second commit. Evaluate a complete audited settlement path that preserves existing evidence authentication and genuine conflicting-value review requirements.
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-14T22:04:28.563Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T16:54:47.558Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T16:52:15.122Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T16:52:15.122Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Reproduce the submitted fresh Git merge on the immutable published artifact and candidate; preserve both branch values and history; validate authenticated no-discard settlement and fresh-clone receipt portability; prove same-field conflicts, lossy decisions, malformed or unsealed legacy evidence remain review-required; retain SDK/CLI parity and non-surprising opt-in hook behavior; do not weaken health or verification merely to suppress a pending state."
parent: pm-dj98
risk: high
confidence: medium
severity: medium
resolution: "Added SDK-backed guarded staging and explicit merge-aware pre-commit hook installation for a paused no-commit/no-ff merge. Required validated portable receipt counterparts before any audit reference, including forced history repair; health no longer accepts clone-local evidence as durable proof. CLI/MCP contracts, narrow SDK docs and native macOS/Windows checks use the same primitives."
expected_result: "Retain both branches and authenticated audit evidence in one reviewed merge commit; refuse nonportable, lossy, untrusted, dirty or alternate-index automatic staging while preserving default hook-free installation."
actual_result: "Real-Git tests preserve lossless values and audited history in the original merge commit, with clean index and fresh-clone health/history parity. Dry-run/apply/force refuse stale local-only evidence before writing history. The immutable published2026.10.18 artifact reproduced the unsafe history reference and fresh-clone failure. All linked tests and231-test driver/install coverage pass; hosted checks will gate merge."
